{
  "plancraftGrid": 1,
  "name": "Spending floor and lifestyle creep grid",
  "description": "An $8,000/mo real spending floor guarantees necessities before legacy: where a legacy target is infeasible, success probability drops (the portfolio cannot fund the floor) or spending pins at the floor. Lifestyle creep is a growing accumulation-phase expense - mild: $500/mo from 2030 growing 8%/yr real ($24k/yr by 2048); strong: $1,000/mo growing 10%/yr ($67k/yr by 2048) - equivalent to an eroding savings rate. Creep ends at retirement; the ratcheted lifestyle expectation itself is not modeled. Fixed: 2 kids public, FERS (7/8, 2023 start) + SS as planned, no disability.",
